      "block_id": "2605.00224_p13_b0",
      "text": "TUR-DPO: Topology- and Uncertainty-Aware Direct Preference Optimization\n",
      "bbox": [
        149.03,
        47.23,
        447.56,
        56.19
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        596,
        188,
        1790,
        224
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 8.97,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Medi",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 71,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.00224_p13_b1",
      "text": "synthesize four candidates per prompt using nucleus sam-\npling with temperature 0.7 and top p 0.95. A calibrated\nLLM judge ranks candidates with side flipping and chain of\nthought hidden during judging. A small verifier suite checks\narithmetic consistency, facts against Wikipedia snapshots,\nand contradiction on paraphrase pairs. We form one pair\nper prompt by selecting the top judged candidate and a hard\nnegative with minimal reference log probability gap, which\nincreases training signal near the decision boundary. To\ncalibrate the judge we sample 200 examples per domain\nand collect double human labels with adjudication, measure\nCohen\u2019s kappa and Kendall\u2019s tau against the judge, and fit a\ntemperature to improve probabilistic calibration. Ties and\nuncertain pairs are kept but will receive smaller weights later.\nWe deduplicate pairs by exact match and by near duplicate\ndetection on embeddings to prevent leakage across splits.\n",
      "bbox": [
        54.97,
        69.39,
        291.19,
        258.76
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        219,
        277,
        1164,
        1035
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 10.06,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 937,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.00224_p13_b2",
      "text": "C.4. Decoupling verifier roles (circularity check)\n",
      "bbox": [
        55.44,
        273.84,
        260.01,
        283.8
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        221,
        1095,
        1040,
        1135
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 9.96,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Medi",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 50,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.00224_p13_b3",
      "text": "To mitigate potential circularity when the same veri-\nfier family contributes to both pair construction (arith-\nmetic/fact/contradiction checks) and training-time weight-\ning (node correctness for uncertainty), we run two controls:\n(a) remove verifier checks from pair construction, relying\nsolely on the calibrated LLM judge for selection; (b) keep\nverifier checks for pair construction but swap to an indepen-\ndent verifier (different model/data) for node-level correct-\nness during training. Qualitatively, (a) increases variance\n(harder negatives, slightly noisier pairs) but preserves the\nrelative gains of TUR-DPO; (b) yields a small calibration\nshift that is corrected by per-domain temperature scaling,\nwith win-rate and ECE trends matching the main results.\n",
      "bbox": [
        55.08,
        292.51,
        291.1,
        446.01
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        220,
        1170,
        1164,
