    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.00224_p13_b23",
      "text": "Because formatting errors increase under TUR-DPO, we\ndeploy a lightweight answer validator at inference time.\nThe validator uses regular expressions to detect missing\nboxed answers in GSM8K/MATH and missing short-form\nanswers in QA. When validation fails, we either re-sample\nwith temperature 0.3 or apply a simple rule-based extraction\n(e.g., extracting the final numeric value for arithmetic tasks).\nTable 16 reports metrics with and without post-processing.\nPost-processing fully mitigates the formatting deficit and\nyields a net improvement of 2.1 EM points on GSM8K\nand 1.4 EM points on QA relative to vanilla DPO without\npost-processing, indicating that the structural gains from\nTUR-DPO are orthogonal to surface-form issues.\n",
      "bbox": [
